WEBVTT

00:00:44.833 --> 00:00:45.958
Neil!

00:00:47.083 --> 00:00:48.375
Neil!

00:00:52.083 --> 00:00:53.375
Neil Spencer!

00:00:53.875 --> 00:00:55.583
Neil Spencer!

00:00:57.833 --> 00:00:59.000
Neil!

00:00:59.833 --> 00:01:01.916
Anything more on the parents?

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.041
Background checks
dug up nothing new.

00:01:04.125 --> 00:01:08.375
Dad's AWOL, mom's in rehab,
grandma's been taking care of the boy.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:09.833
All right.

00:01:10.333 --> 00:01:12.458
I want all interviews
with immediate family in the area

00:01:12.541 --> 00:01:13.750
complete by the end of the day.

00:01:13.833 --> 00:01:15.083
Yes, Detective.

00:01:16.333 --> 00:01:17.291
Neil!

00:01:17.916 --> 00:01:20.000
-Neil!
- This is not a race.

00:01:20.083 --> 00:01:22.333
Take your time.
We're looking for a missing child.

00:01:22.416 --> 00:01:24.000
All right, people.

00:01:24.541 --> 00:01:25.458
Listen up!

00:01:25.541 --> 00:01:28.708
All right, Neil Spencer was put to bed
around 8:00 p.m. last night.

00:01:28.791 --> 00:01:32.791
His grandmother reported him missing
at 10:29 p.m.

00:01:32.875 --> 00:01:35.958
Be prepared to call your families
and let them know you won't be home.

00:01:36.041 --> 00:01:38.583
Detective! We found something.

00:02:08.833 --> 00:02:10.625
This isn't Neil Spencer.

00:02:29.083 --> 00:02:32.083
["Shiny Happy People" by R.E.M.
playing over radio]

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:36.666
♪ Meet me in the crowd… ♪

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:39.583
You know, I'm excited.
It's a fresh start, right?

00:02:41.625 --> 00:02:42.625
-Yeah?
-Yeah.

00:02:42.708 --> 00:02:46.166
You know, your mom always wanted us
to move back to the town we grew up in.

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:49.791
You know, it's cool. You'll be going
to the same school she did. Right?

00:02:49.875 --> 00:02:51.083
-Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:02:52.083 --> 00:02:54.208
Plus, we found a house with a swing.

00:02:54.291 --> 00:02:57.541
I mean, it's just like the one
you guys loved at the shore.

00:02:57.625 --> 00:02:59.375
You've said.

00:02:59.458 --> 00:03:00.958
Like a thousand times.

00:03:01.041 --> 00:03:02.625
No, no, no. No, that's incorrect.

00:03:02.708 --> 00:03:04.791
I've only said it 936 times.

00:03:04.875 --> 00:03:06.833
-
- So get your facts straight.

00:03:11.708 --> 00:03:13.000
I miss her.

00:03:15.916 --> 00:03:17.083
Me too, buddy.

00:03:19.791 --> 00:03:22.916
Up! Get your legs up.
Get 'em up. Come on. Up, up, up, up, up!

00:03:24.208 --> 00:03:27.333
And… we are in Garretton.

00:03:27.416 --> 00:03:29.125
♪ Everyone around… ♪

00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:30.166
We did it.

00:03:30.875 --> 00:03:34.791
♪ Love them, love them ♪

00:03:34.875 --> 00:03:38.375
♪ Put it in your hands ♪

00:03:38.458 --> 00:03:42.208
♪ Take it, take it… ♪

00:03:59.208 --> 00:04:00.333
There it is.

00:04:01.833 --> 00:04:03.125
-Wanna go check it out?
-Yeah.

00:04:03.208 --> 00:04:04.083
Go ahead.

00:04:05.625 --> 00:04:06.875
-Hey, guys.
- What's up?

00:04:06.958 --> 00:04:10.041
Hey, how you doing?
Uh, where do you want these, sir?

00:04:10.125 --> 00:04:13.166
Yeah, you know what?
Those can go in the kitchen. Thank you.

00:04:19.416 --> 00:04:22.375
- Hey, Dad! Look at this!
-Be right there, buddy.

00:04:32.083 --> 00:04:34.583
I hope this place is
big enough for you, Jake.

00:04:48.541 --> 00:04:51.625
All right, come on, kiddo.
We got a new house, new stairs.

00:04:51.708 --> 00:04:53.250
What did we say we were gonna be?

00:04:55.708 --> 00:04:56.833
Brave.

00:04:57.333 --> 00:04:58.458
That's right.

00:04:59.083 --> 00:05:01.375
Just like your mom when she was sick.

00:05:03.541 --> 00:05:04.375
Come here.

00:05:06.125 --> 00:05:09.333
All right. Let's go upstairs.

00:05:09.958 --> 00:05:11.083
Yeah.

00:05:15.166 --> 00:05:17.125
And…

00:05:17.958 --> 00:05:19.083
Go find your room.

00:05:49.625 --> 00:05:50.833
What's wrong?

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:54.000
Why are you so scared?

00:05:57.166 --> 00:05:58.458
It's gonna be fine.

00:06:02.583 --> 00:06:05.083
No, not… No! Wait a second.

00:06:05.166 --> 00:06:06.291
You can't take him.

00:06:06.375 --> 00:06:07.916
Okay, Saturn's going…

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.041
Do-do-do-do-do-do!

00:06:10.125 --> 00:06:11.041
…right up to the sun.

00:06:11.125 --> 00:06:12.041
Do-do-do-do!

00:06:12.125 --> 00:06:13.625
- No!
- Chain reaction.

00:06:13.708 --> 00:06:14.541
No!

00:06:14.625 --> 00:06:16.333
Oh no!

00:06:19.625 --> 00:06:21.000
All right. Uh…

00:06:21.083 --> 00:06:22.666
-Okay. You ready?
- Yeah.

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:24.750
Good? It's gonna be great. Okay?

00:06:26.041 --> 00:06:29.166
You warm enough?
Yeah? Wanna hang onto that?

00:06:29.916 --> 00:06:30.750
You sure?

00:06:31.708 --> 00:06:32.833
Yeah?

00:06:32.916 --> 00:06:33.958
Okay. All right.

00:06:34.041 --> 00:06:35.083
Come here.

00:06:36.125 --> 00:06:38.208
All right. Have a good day, okay?

00:06:38.291 --> 00:06:40.625
I'm gonna be right here
when school gets out, all right?

00:06:41.125 --> 00:06:43.375
-Okay. Okay?
-Hmm.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:34.166
Oh fuck.

00:07:41.166 --> 00:07:42.500
Jesus.

00:08:18.541 --> 00:08:21.083
If your window's left unlatched

00:08:21.916 --> 00:08:24.375
You'll hear him tapping at the glass

00:09:54.583 --> 00:09:56.583
What kind of fish were they?

00:09:57.083 --> 00:09:58.541
I don't know.

00:09:58.625 --> 00:10:02.041
There was a pink one. And a blue one.

00:10:02.958 --> 00:10:04.916
Do you think
they'll miss you?

00:10:05.708 --> 00:10:07.208
My fish?

00:10:07.291 --> 00:10:10.541
You fed them, right?
Like your daddy fed you.

00:10:11.041 --> 00:10:14.291
Do you think they'll miss you
feeding them?

00:10:15.625 --> 00:10:18.208
- I don't know.
- Speak up, boy.

00:10:18.791 --> 00:10:21.041
What if they get hungry
and you're not there?

00:10:21.541 --> 00:10:23.500
Do you think they'll eat each other?

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:28.541
When one fish is shitting out the other,
will they be thinking of you?

00:10:37.458 --> 00:10:38.625
Good.

00:10:39.916 --> 00:10:42.416
Good. I think they're going to love this.

00:10:47.041 --> 00:10:48.458
That's for later.

00:11:29.791 --> 00:11:31.166
Hi, Mr. Willis.

00:11:31.666 --> 00:11:34.041
Uh, Detective Amanda Beck, Garretton PD.

00:11:34.541 --> 00:11:35.500
May I come in?

00:11:36.666 --> 00:11:38.416
I'm sorry to interrupt your dinner.

00:11:39.041 --> 00:11:42.208
Uh, a boy went missing
in Hillcrest a couple of days ago.

00:11:42.291 --> 00:11:43.541
Neil Spencer.

00:11:43.625 --> 00:11:46.166
We've cleared locations,
family, and friends.

00:11:46.791 --> 00:11:50.541
We found something, and I don't know
if it's a lead or a distraction.

00:11:54.583 --> 00:11:56.458
Another body. A boy.

00:11:56.541 --> 00:11:58.458
Been out in the woods about a month.

00:12:04.666 --> 00:12:06.708
Not every kid
who disappears in North Jersey

00:12:06.791 --> 00:12:08.708
is connected to Frank Carter, Detective.

00:12:08.791 --> 00:12:10.666
But that's his signature, right?

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:13.291
Well, Frank Carter's doing life
in Rahway now.

00:12:14.208 --> 00:12:15.333
That's not what I asked.

00:12:17.041 --> 00:12:20.833
I know you need to find him, of course,
but I don't know if I can help you.

00:12:20.916 --> 00:12:22.958
The other boy who went missing,
Neil Spencer,

00:12:23.041 --> 00:12:26.833
told his grandma he heard a strange voice
outside his window

00:12:27.666 --> 00:12:28.958
whispering to him.

00:12:31.625 --> 00:12:34.291
Well, you know,
kids have active imaginations--

00:12:34.375 --> 00:12:36.958
Yes, that's what Carter preyed on.
That's what you said.

00:12:37.041 --> 00:12:39.125
I did, but, you know,
I'm not on the job anymore.

00:12:39.208 --> 00:12:42.000
It's been a long time.
I'm retired at least 25 years.

00:12:42.083 --> 00:12:44.291
I just, you know…
And there's only one Frank Carter.

00:12:44.375 --> 00:12:48.750
Your case file mentioned an accomplice
to Carter who was never identified.

00:12:48.833 --> 00:12:51.333
I did. I did.
It was a theory, and it went cold.

00:12:51.416 --> 00:12:52.416
They often do.

00:12:59.791 --> 00:13:02.875
Frank Carter still declines all interviews
via his lawyers.

00:13:02.958 --> 00:13:05.416
You remain the only one
he's ever agreed to speak with

00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:08.458
since his, uh, incarceration.

00:13:09.583 --> 00:13:11.375
Got any advice interviewing him?

00:13:11.458 --> 00:13:13.250
Yeah, I'd say don't.

00:13:16.041 --> 00:13:18.000
I… I hope you find your kid.

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:21.375
With all due respect, sir,
hope does nothing for me.

00:13:57.666 --> 00:14:00.625
Can I put this
in my Packet of Special Things?

00:14:00.708 --> 00:14:02.125
Let me see.

00:14:07.625 --> 00:14:08.458
Sure.

00:14:15.333 --> 00:14:16.541
What's that?

00:14:17.208 --> 00:14:19.791
We made our hands be in paint
on the wall at school.

00:14:19.875 --> 00:14:21.583
Oh, yeah? Handprints, huh?

00:14:21.666 --> 00:14:23.041
- Mm-hmm.
-Cool.

00:14:23.125 --> 00:14:24.500
My friend helped me.

00:14:26.291 --> 00:14:28.333
Oh, yeah? You make a friend?

00:14:29.333 --> 00:14:31.041
The girl in the blue sweater.

00:14:33.250 --> 00:14:35.958
Well, do you remember
we talked about that?

00:14:36.041 --> 00:14:38.416
How some friends are pretend and…

00:14:42.458 --> 00:14:43.625
What's up, bud?

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:47.958
Are you sure she won't wake up?

00:14:48.041 --> 00:14:49.000
Mommy?

00:14:50.416 --> 00:14:51.541
I am.

00:14:53.958 --> 00:14:56.291
You know, Mommy loved you

00:14:57.458 --> 00:15:01.625
more than anything, you know,
and that's… that's never gonna change.

00:15:02.166 --> 00:15:06.250
But it doesn't mean
that you can't make room for new people,

00:15:06.333 --> 00:15:08.625
you know, new… new friends.

00:15:09.291 --> 00:15:11.833
I don't like the boys at school.

00:15:15.083 --> 00:15:16.000
You know,

00:15:16.916 --> 00:15:18.375
I never told you this,

00:15:18.458 --> 00:15:23.416
but when I was your age,
I had a friend, just like you have.

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:24.416
I did.

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:27.666
He'd visit me when I was going to sleep,
and we'd go on adventures.

00:15:28.333 --> 00:15:29.875
At the end, every time,

00:15:29.958 --> 00:15:32.375
he would kiss me on the forehead,
right here.

00:15:32.458 --> 00:15:33.541
And then

00:15:34.416 --> 00:15:38.375
I'd wake up the next morning
back in bed like magic.

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:41.375
I called him Mr. Night.

00:15:43.333 --> 00:15:46.208
It's okay to imagine things, Jake.

00:15:46.291 --> 00:15:48.041
You just… You gotta

00:15:48.958 --> 00:15:51.583
give real people a chance, too, okay?

00:16:17.958 --> 00:16:19.541
What is your name?

00:16:25.833 --> 00:16:27.083
It's okay.

00:16:28.208 --> 00:16:29.916
They need to hear this.

00:17:26.708 --> 00:17:29.291
Hey! Sorry! Sorry, I'm late.

00:17:29.375 --> 00:17:32.333
-You're Jake's father?
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. Hi. How you doing?

00:17:33.125 --> 00:17:34.500
Buddy, what's wrong?

00:17:34.583 --> 00:17:36.750
You wanna tell your dad
what happened?

00:17:37.541 --> 00:17:39.250
I got put on yellow.

00:17:39.333 --> 00:17:40.625
You… On what?

00:17:40.708 --> 00:17:43.208
We have a traffic light system
for bad behavior.

00:17:43.791 --> 00:17:45.916
What'd he do? Uh, what'd you do?

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:49.125
Owen tried to take
my Packet of Special Things.

00:17:49.208 --> 00:17:51.583
He scratched a boy. Badly.

00:17:51.666 --> 00:17:54.875
Okay, well, that's…
You can't do that, Jake.

00:17:54.958 --> 00:17:57.416
Um, sorry. It's this packet.

00:17:57.500 --> 00:18:01.125
Um, it's full of stuff that,
like, belonged to his mom.

00:18:01.208 --> 00:18:02.666
That's no excuse.

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:06.500
We'd like him to write a note apologizing.

00:18:07.833 --> 00:18:09.666
Uh, isn't that excessive?

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:12.250
We have zero tolerance
for kids hurting kids.

00:18:12.333 --> 00:18:13.875
What's your tolerance for bullies?

00:18:13.958 --> 00:18:16.416
'Cause that other kid
sounds like kind of a dick.

00:18:16.500 --> 00:18:19.416
- Excuse me?
-You know what? We'll pass on that note.

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:20.416
Come on, buddy.

00:18:21.583 --> 00:18:23.166
You can put me on yellow.

00:18:29.708 --> 00:18:30.666
Where is it?

00:18:35.666 --> 00:18:38.750
I didn't like being there,

00:18:38.833 --> 00:18:40.458
that house.

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:42.708
Your grandmother's.

00:18:43.583 --> 00:18:45.708
Was she mean to you?

00:18:46.750 --> 00:18:49.208
No. Sometimes

00:18:49.833 --> 00:18:51.458
she was sick.

00:18:52.875 --> 00:18:54.375
I was afraid.

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:56.416
It's okay.

00:18:57.208 --> 00:18:59.041
They need to hear it.

00:19:00.750 --> 00:19:03.083
I was afraid she'd die.

00:19:03.166 --> 00:19:06.958
She'd be dead in the house with me
while I slept.

00:19:08.208 --> 00:19:11.333
If you could talk to your mommy
right now,

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:13.666
what would you say?

00:19:15.958 --> 00:19:18.083
Why did you leave me there?

00:19:18.791 --> 00:19:20.583
Why don't you love me?

00:19:22.208 --> 00:19:23.625
I love you.

00:19:26.250 --> 00:19:30.250
♪ Free your mind
And the rest will follow ♪

00:19:30.791 --> 00:19:33.166
♪ Be color blind ♪

00:19:33.250 --> 00:19:34.916
♪ Don't be so shallow ♪

00:19:35.875 --> 00:19:39.916
♪ Free your mind
And the rest will follow ♪

00:20:51.166 --> 00:20:54.041
If you leave a door half open

00:20:54.125 --> 00:20:56.750
Soon you'll hear the whispers spoken

00:20:57.458 --> 00:20:59.625
If your window is left unlatched

00:20:59.708 --> 00:21:02.166
You'll hear him tapping at the glass

00:21:03.208 --> 00:21:04.250
Jake?

00:21:05.625 --> 00:21:06.833
What are you doing?

00:21:11.583 --> 00:21:12.500
Jake!

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:14.625
No!

00:21:27.625 --> 00:21:28.916
Who were you talking to?

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:30.333
Nobody.

00:21:45.291 --> 00:21:46.208
Back to bed.

00:22:46.708 --> 00:22:47.750
Hey!

00:22:50.791 --> 00:22:53.083
Hey! What are you doing?

00:22:53.166 --> 00:22:55.500
Hey! Hey! Hey!

00:23:01.958 --> 00:23:05.791
We've had reports of a squatter
since the place went vacant.

00:23:05.875 --> 00:23:09.958
Kids sneaking in to drink
and do other things.

00:23:10.041 --> 00:23:11.625
This wasn't a kid.

00:23:14.125 --> 00:23:15.000
What's back here?

00:23:16.583 --> 00:23:17.708
I don't know.

00:23:24.125 --> 00:23:26.041
-Holy shit.
- Ooh.

00:23:30.750 --> 00:23:32.083
-Whoa.
-Previous owner?

00:23:32.583 --> 00:23:33.541
Um…

00:23:35.166 --> 00:23:36.333
So now what?

00:23:37.583 --> 00:23:39.208
Well, he didn't attack you.

00:23:39.291 --> 00:23:42.291
He just bolted for the door
unless there's something else.

00:23:42.375 --> 00:23:44.750
He's most likely just a squatter.

00:23:45.375 --> 00:23:46.833
Left something here.

00:23:46.916 --> 00:23:49.125
Didn't realize the place was rented.

00:23:49.208 --> 00:23:51.166
Change the locks,
set up a security system,

00:23:51.250 --> 00:23:53.333
and donate this stuff to the Goodwill.

00:23:53.833 --> 00:23:55.875
And don't forget to bolt your back door.

00:23:58.208 --> 00:23:59.291
So that's it?

00:23:59.791 --> 00:24:02.666
Fresh coat of paint
on the outside might help ward people off.

00:24:53.583 --> 00:24:56.250
If you're lonely, sad, and blue

00:24:56.333 --> 00:24:58.666
The Whisper Man will come for you

00:25:04.958 --> 00:25:07.000
If your window's
left unlatched

00:25:07.083 --> 00:25:08.916
You'll hear him tapping at the…

00:25:09.000 --> 00:25:10.583
Jake, what are you doing?

00:25:10.666 --> 00:25:11.875
Nothing.

00:25:17.458 --> 00:25:18.416
Okay.

00:25:19.125 --> 00:25:20.500
Who are you talking to?

00:25:22.750 --> 00:25:24.333
Is it the girl in the blue sweater?

00:25:27.791 --> 00:25:30.708
She's scared of it here.

00:25:30.791 --> 00:25:33.208
She's scared of it here?
She's scared of this house? Why?

00:25:34.208 --> 00:25:36.250
She's scared of the boy who lives here.

00:25:37.416 --> 00:25:38.333
You?

00:25:40.125 --> 00:25:41.000
Who?

00:25:41.083 --> 00:25:42.458
The boy in the floor.

00:25:42.541 --> 00:25:44.958
The boy in the floor. Good God.

00:25:45.041 --> 00:25:47.333
Jake, you have to stop this.

00:25:47.416 --> 00:25:48.500
Stop what?

00:25:48.583 --> 00:25:51.000
Well… Ow! Goddammit!

00:25:52.541 --> 00:25:55.375
Pretending. I need you to grow up.

00:25:55.458 --> 00:25:57.041
You never believe me.

00:25:57.125 --> 00:25:58.250
I can see you.

00:25:58.333 --> 00:25:59.833
I can see everything,

00:25:59.916 --> 00:26:03.041
and I know there is no one in here, Jake.

00:26:03.125 --> 00:26:05.750
You are just talking to yourself.

00:26:51.208 --> 00:26:52.166
Jake?

00:26:56.875 --> 00:26:57.791
Wha…

00:27:05.875 --> 00:27:06.958
Jake?

00:27:09.875 --> 00:27:11.083
Jake!

00:27:11.166 --> 00:27:12.041
Jake!

00:27:13.208 --> 00:27:14.166
Jake!

00:27:15.208 --> 00:27:16.166
Jake!

00:27:20.500 --> 00:27:21.916
Jake!

00:27:25.375 --> 00:27:26.291
Jake!

00:27:27.875 --> 00:27:29.958
Jake!

00:27:31.041 --> 00:27:32.208
Jake!

00:27:33.375 --> 00:27:34.416
Jake!

00:27:59.333 --> 00:28:02.375
I'm Detective Beck.
Tell me a little bit about Jake.

00:28:04.458 --> 00:28:05.416
Okay.

00:28:07.500 --> 00:28:08.416
I know.

00:28:09.625 --> 00:28:11.375
-It's terrifying.
-

00:28:13.666 --> 00:28:14.750
He's quiet.

00:28:15.250 --> 00:28:16.250
It's hard.

00:28:17.375 --> 00:28:20.708
But we don't know which detail
is gonna help us find him.

